# Explainer video pipeline (locked mix)

New Healthings explainers (prompt107, phone-health, CGM, habit clips) match the **Activity
YouTube** cut — same voice, same instrumental bed, steady picture. Do not re-audition voices
or invent a new music bed unless the owner asks.

## Locked defaults

| Knob | Value |
|------|--------|
| VO | ElevenLabs **Matilda** — alias `matilda`, id `XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX` |
| Subs (social default) | Hebrew burned on EN VO (`subs_lang: he`) |
| Sub look | **Outline only** (navy fill + thick white edge) — no 0.3 full-width band |
| Sub font | **Noto Sans Hebrew** (HE burns) / **Noto Sans** (Latin) in `assets/fonts/` |
| Music bed | `FB/videos/assets/audio/music/gym-max-oazo-bed-novocals.mp3` (instrumental) |
| Bed level | `--music-level 0.18` (pre-duck); sidechain duck keeps VO on top |
| Picture | **Steady film** — `--motion 1.0` (default). No Ken Burns / zoompan on UI stills |
| Loudness | `-14` LUFS via `render_clip.py` loudnorm |
| Aspect | `9x16` primary |

## Locale ladder (product — clarity over completeness)

Ship speed and first-session clarity beat “10 dubbed Netflix catalogs.”

| Tier | What | When |
|------|------|------|
| **0 — Master** | EN Matilda VO + HE burned subs + instrumental + steady | Every new clip before anything else |
| **1 — Permission literacy** | **FR + DE spoken VO** (Matilda multilingual) for `phone-health` + `cgm-pipeline` only | After EN masters exist — Europe clinic / setup confusion |
| **2 — Habit clips** | FR/DE VO for meal / activity only if Tier 1 proved watch time | Optional |
| **HE spoken VO** | **Do not** — HE burned on EN only (prior HE VO quality fail) | Reopen only with a Hebrew-native audition win |
| **Other app locales** (es, pt, it, ar, ru, tr) | Catalog titles localized; video stays EN (+ HE burns on social) | No dubbed VO until a named market pull |

**In-app Watch URL:** prefer `appLocale` cut when hosted (`…/fr/watch/phone-health`); else fall back to EN master. Never block setup on a missing locale file.

**Why FR/DE VO (not subs-only) for permission films:** write→read / xDrip / Health Connect is easy to miss while reading burned lines over English speech. Spoken local language wins clarity; meal how-tos can stay EN+subs longer.

The vocal bed `gym-max-oazo-bed.mp3` is legacy A/B only — **prefer `-novocals`** so Matilda
does not fight sung lyrics.

## Canonical render

```powershell
python FB/videos/elevenlabs/gen_clip_vo.py --clip <id> --voice matilda --tag matilda --force
python FB/videos/production/render_clip.py --clip <id> `
  --vo-tag matilda `
  --music FB/videos/assets/audio/music/gym-max-oazo-bed-novocals.mp3 `
  --music-level 0.18
  # --motion 1.0 is already the default — omit unless overriding
```

Primary export: copy/rename the `-matilda` cut to the untagged `…-en-subhe-9x16.mp4` when the
owner accepts it (same pattern as clip 07).

## Steady film — what it means

- Still phone UI stays **sharp and locked** (`motion <= 1.0`)
- Screencap / B-roll video may move on its own; do **not** add zoompan on top
- Soft push (`--motion 1.06`) only if the owner asks for a living-still beat

## Don't

- Default new clips to Daniel / Sarah / other audition voices
- Render without `--music` when shipping a social cut (bed is part of the brand mix now)
- Use the vocal Max Oazo bed as the default
- Re-enable Ken Burns “to make it feel alive” without an explicit ask
- Full-width low-opacity subtitle bands (0.3) — outline only unless a still fails readability
- Dub all 10 app locales before EN masters + FR/DE permission VO
- Reopen Hebrew spoken VO without a native-voice audition win
- Embed mp4s in the app APK (prompt107 — URLs only)

